{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
  "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals held that the definition of crime of violence in 18 U.S.C 16(b) is unconstitutionally vague on its face, relying on this Court's decision in Johnson, holding the residual clause in the Armed Career Criminal Act unconstitutionally vague."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT, MR. KNEEDLER, DIDN'T THE GOVERNMENT ARGUE IN -- WHEN JOHNSON WAS BEFORE US, THAT IF THE ACCA RESIDUAL CLAUSE WAS INVALID, THEN 16(b) WOULD BE VULNERABLE BECAUSE IT WAS SUBJECT TO THE SAME CENTRAL OBJECTION. WASN'T THAT THE GOVERNMENT'S ARGUMENT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WELL, MAY I ASK, MR. KNEEDLER, BECAUSE THIS ASPECT OF YOUR BRIEF WAS CONFUSING TO ME BECAUSE SOMETIMES YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT TEMPORAL, AND SOMETIMES YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT FUNCTIONAL. AND I WANT TO KNOW WHAT YOU THINK THE REAL LIMITATION IS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "VEHICULAR FLIGHT FROM A POLICE OFFICER AFTER BEING ORDERED TO STOP IS, AGAIN, IF YOU THINK BY ITS NATURE, WHAT -- WHAT WAS THE LEGISLATURE ENVISIONING WHEN IT ENACTED THAT? AND I THINK, AGAIN, IT'S PARALLEL TO BURGLARY."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I REMEMBER THE GOVERNMENT ARGUING IN JOHNSON THAT MOST PEOPLE WHO ARE FOUND WITH SAWED-OFF SHOTGUNS ARE COMMITTING CRIMES. WHY ISN'T THAT A SUBSTANTIAL RISK OF FORCE BEING USED?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If the Court -- if the Court were to hold that 16(b) is unconstitutionally vague in criminal cases, what would the impact -- in criminal cases involving the application of the categorical approach, what would the -- what would the implications of that be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Well, as we cite in our brief, there are a number of places in Title 18 where the definition of crime of violence is used, either by express reference to 16(b) or by use of the same formulation like in 924C where the same formulation is -- is used."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But I thought the point the Chief Justice is underscoring is that if we go -- if we base the decision on the fact that -- that this is civil, then you have to come back here for other cases under --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KNEEDLER: Right. I think DUI is sort -- is the prime example. Leocal itself concluded that DUI was not covered. In -- in a unanimous opinion, it's only -- the Court's only occasion to have to address this in 30 years because of the text of 16(b), the act -- it requires the act of use of force."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENKRANZ: Well, Justice Kagan, let me -- let me give two answers. The first is that this whole notion that the government is discussing about a different experience with ACCA than with Section 16(b) is revisionist history."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But what of the argument that 16(b) is more precise? For one thing, it is"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So to the extent that we're focusing on language that appears in the immigration statutes, that language has been interpreted. And that is a key distinction between this case and Mahler, for example, with -- with -- which Mr. Kneedler invoked."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mahler was a situation in which Congress had defined the crimes that would make you deportable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, so, Justice Alito, this Court in Hoffman said that it's a sliding scale. But in Jordan, when it came to deportation, which this Court has described as the gravest sort of consequence which directly implicates liberty interests, this Court said it's at the same level as --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, would you say the same thing if it didn't -- if this statute did not incorporate a definition that is also used in criminal statutes and simply had the same standard in a purely immigration statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's why this case didn't work under 16(a) and the elements, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the principle of law that led to A.B. Small? No one thinks statutory words in the civil context, \"unjust or unreasonable rates,\" whether enforced by courts against railroads, or whether enforced by an agency, is unconstitutional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "445d04fab54520e12844efd48cf058ec149f9bfe4381a3602c39b12d48f47d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-445d04fab545-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
